---
name: react
description: >
  Real model prompt (issue #370): a walking agent that newly notices another
  resident is asked -- via the `react` tool -- whether to keep going
  ("continue"), pause for a hello ("greet", which starts a #371 multi-tick
  conversation), or change the rest of its day ("replan"). Rendered by
  cognition._consult_react(), only when a real tool-calling brain is wired --
  the rule tier and the brain-identity gate keep the mock bake byte-identical.
inputs:
  partner:
    type: string
    description: The name of the resident who came into view.
  doing:
    type: string
    description: What this agent is in the middle of.
  time:
    type: string
    description: Preformatted sim time of day, or omitted when the run has no clock.
  memories:
    type: array
    description: What this agent remembers about the partner (may be empty).
sample:
  partner: Ayesha Khan
  doing: walking to Van Pelt Library
  time: Monday 09:30 AM
  memories:
    - Ayesha Khan is my study partner.
---
{%- if time %}It is {{ time }}. {% endif %}While {{ doing }}, you notice {{ partner }} nearby.
{%- if memories %}
What you remember about {{ partner }}:
{% for m in memories %}
- {{ m }}
{% endfor %}
{%- endif %}
Decide how to react: keep going ("continue"), stop for a quick hello ("greet"), or change your plans for the rest of the day ("replan"). Greet or replan only if it feels natural for you -- your schedule matters.
